 The BFD 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Brendan Lynch/Axios

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Piper Sandler (NYSE: PIPR) is in talks to buy advisory firm Perella Weinberg Partners (Nasdaq: PWP), per the WSJ. 

 Why it's the BFD: Bank consolidation is nothing new — Piper Sandler itself is the result of a 2020 merger — but this reflects how many boutique advisories are struggling to defend their niches.

 By the numbers: Piper Sandler shares fell nearly 10% yesterday on the news, giving it a $4.6 billion market cap.

 Perella Weinberg shares surged nearly 12%, pushing its market cap above $1.5 billion. The bottom line: "Perella Weinberg did a series of its own deals over the years. Earlier this year, it struck a deal for the U.K.-based advisory firm Gleacher Shacklock, and last year it agreed to acquire secondary advisory firm Devon Park Advisors. The bank previously bought the energy-focused boutique bank Tudor Pickering Holt in 2016." — Lauren Thomas &amp; AnnaMaria Andriotis, WSJ 

 
 
